COMMON STRING METHODS
Upper()
This returns new string into all capital letters/ Uppercase 
my_str = 'Hello Worls' 
upper_case_my_str = my_str. upper()
print(upper_case_my_str) # HELLO WORLD 

lower() : works similar to upper(), but it converts all letters to lowercase 

STRIP() 
returns a new string with front and back characters removed 
my_str = ' Hello World '  
my_str_stripped = my_str.strip()
print(my_str_striped) # Hello World - spaces infront and back were removed 

REPLACE
replace(old, new) 
my_str = 'Hello World'
my_str_replace = my_str.replace("Hello", "Hi")
print(my_str_replace)  # Hi world 
